🧠 mental model.
from exercise 5, we already have a pony in race template of race component(which we got by binding the
input property raceModel of race component in the races template of races component). 

In order to dynamically assign the pony gifs according to the pony's color, computed signal is the best.
computed signal is read only and derives from other signal. 

So first let's create an input signal 'ponyModel' in our newly created Pony component. The reason behind
the input() is that we need to get the pony from race template into our new Pony component. Hence we are
gonna bind this input signal property ponyModel in the race template just like we bind the raceModel in
the races template in order to passdown the race value in Race component from Races Component in Exercise5.

Great now we have a input() property ponyModel with the value pony. Next part is to create a computed
signal using the pony which has a color property. Now we just created a ponyImageUrl which is a computed
signal using a ponyModel property which is also a signal(remember the definition of computed signal?).

We now have pony image url according to its color. let's do the property binding [src] = "ponyImageUrl()"
and [alt]="ponyModel().name" in the img tag of our pony template.

Next thing we want is our pony component to fire custon event when the user click on the element. Let's
add a click event listener in the root element of our pony template which calls the selectPony() method
in our component. We want this method to emit the ponyModel. Data flows out of the components via events
and custom events are emitted by output(). So let's create an output property 'ponySelected'. Finally we
can emit the ponyModel with value pony using the output property 'ponySelected' when the user clicks on
the element as:

        protected selectPony(): void {
            this.ponySelected.emit(this.ponyModel());
        }

For now, parent component doesn't listen to our custom event but it soon it will. Just for the idea, our
output property 'ponySelected' is the actual event fired when uses clicks the on the element and
ponyModel with the value pony is the value($event) of the event. In parent component's template:
        
        <ns-pony [ponyModel]="ponyModel()" (ponySelected)="betOnPony($event)" />

here, $event is a pony.